I would like to propose a database-level solution to address defect 2156187 , with the following objectives:
1.	Prevent multiple OPEN cash stock sessions for the same cash_stock.
2.	Enforce strict validation on: 
o	status (only OPEN / CLOSE)
o	session_type (currently limited to BRANCH)
Below is the proposed approach and corresponding SQL scripts.
1) Unique constraint for OPEN sessions
To ensure that only one OPEN session can exist per cash stock, we introduce a partial unique index:
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX uk_cash_stock_session_simultaneous_open
ON own_87929_kash.cash_stock_session(cash_stock_id)
WHERE status = 'OPEN';
Expected behavior:
•	Multiple CLOSED sessions remain allowed (history preserved)
•	Any attempt to create a second OPEN session will be rejected
→ Database error: SQLSTATE 23505
•	Backend handling: map this error to the existing business error
KASH_10001011 ("Multiple processes cannot access the CashStock Open simultaneously")
2) CHECK constraints for data integrity
To enforce valid values for status and session_type:
-- Enforce status = 'OPEN' or 'CLOSE'
ALTER TABLE own_87929_kash.cash_stock_session
ADD CONSTRAINT chk_cash_stock_session_status
CHECK (status IN ('OPEN', 'CLOSE'));

-- Enforce session_type = 'BRANCH' only (extendable later)
ALTER TABLE own_87929_kash.cash_stock_session
ADD CONSTRAINT chk_cash_stock_session_type
CHECK (session_type = 'BRANCH');
Expected behavior:
•	Invalid values (e.g. status = 'PENDING') will be rejected
→ Database error: SQLSTATE 23514
•	Backend should treat this as a technical validation error
3) Pre-deployment checks
Before applying the constraints, we need to validate existing data:
-- Check for duplicate OPEN sessions (to be resolved manually if found)
SELECT cash_stock_id, COUNT(*)
FROM own_87929_kash.cash_stock_session
WHERE status = 'OPEN'
GROUP BY cash_stock_id
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;

-- Check for invalid status values
SELECT DISTINCT status
FROM own_87929_kash.cash_stock_session
WHERE status NOT IN ('OPEN', 'CLOSE');

-- Check for invalid session_type values
SELECT DISTINCT session_type
FROM own_87929_kash.cash_stock_session
WHERE session_type != 'BRANCH';

